    "temperature": {
      "file": "air_preheater_temperature.glb",
      "title": "Hot side vs cold side of the rotor",
      "description": "The matrix plates in the gas half (right) are heated by the flue gas; as the rotor turns (about 1–3 rpm) they move into the air half (left) and give that heat to the combustion air. Hotter combustion air improves boiler efficiency (roughly 1 % fuel saving per ~20 °C of extra air temperature, rule of thumb). Leakage of air into gas past the seals is the main performance loss.",
